        "original_id": "ece7e2cf-62e3-58b2-b449-f3eb9f9fe3ec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Wesley, Charles Wesley, George Whitefield, Edward Perronet\n- Organizations: Church of England, Methodism\n- Concepts: 18th-century revival, separate denomination\n\nFacts:\n- John Wesley was born on 28 June 1703 and died on 2 March 1791.\n- John Wesley was an English Anglican cleric and theologian.\n- John Wesley, his brother Charles Wesley, and fellow cleric George Whitefield founded Methodism.\n- Methodism originated as a revival within the 18th-century Church of England.\n- Edward Perronet was born in 1726 and died on 2 January 1792.\n- Edward Perronet was the son of an Anglican priest.\n- Edward Perronet worked closely with Anglican priest John Wesley and his brother Charles Wesley for many years during England's eighteenth-century revival.\n- Methodism became a separate denomination after John Wesley's death.",
